{
    "esm": "1.0.0",
    "models": {
        "IgnitionComponent": {
            "variables": {
                "QIGN": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Heat of ignition (dimensionless)"
                },
                "CHI": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Intermediate variable (dimensionless)"
                },
                "MC1": {
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "1-hour fuel moisture content (dimensionless)"
                },
                "TMPPRM": {
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Temperature at fuel-atmosphere interface"
                },
                "SC": {
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Spread component"
                },
                "PI": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Probability of ignition 0-100 (dimensionless)"
                },
                "PFI": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Probability of reportable fire given ignition (dimensionless)"
                },
                "V_ref": {
                    "default": 1,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Reference velocity for non-dimensionalization"
                },
                "K_ref": {
                    "default": 1,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Reference temperature for non-dimensionalization"
                },
                "SCM": {
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Spread component threshold for reportable fires"
                },
                "IC": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Ignition component 0-100 (dimensionless)"
                },
                "SCN": {
                    "type": "unknown",
                    "description": "Normalized spread component (dimensionless)"
                },
                "PNORM3": {
                    "default": 1.85e-05,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "P(I) scaling factor 3 (dimensionless)"
                },
                "PNORM1": {
                    "default": 0.00232,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "P(I) scaling factor 1 (dimensionless)"
                },
                "PNORM2": {
                    "default": 0.99767,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "P(I) scaling factor 2 (dimensionless)"
                },
                "K_to_C": {
                    "default": 273.15,
                    "type": "parameter",
                    "description": "Kelvin to Celsius offset (dimensionless)"
                }
            },
            "reference": {
                "notes": "source_ref: WildlandFire.jl/src/nfdrs.jl:1291\nNFDRS Ignition Component (IC) - calculates probability of ignition and reportable fire\n\nTODO_GAP: gt-p3ep - registered function needed for 'max' operator\nTODO_GAP: gt-p3ep - registered function needed for 'min' operator\n\nTest inputs are parameters and go in `parameter_overrides`. They were previously written as `initial_conditions`, which do not set parameters (and which leave MC1, TMPPRM, SC and SCM, none of which has a default, without a value: esm-spec §10.10), and the stored expected values (IC = 0 in every test, the same P(I) for two different inputs) did not correspond to the inputs. They are now the closed-form values for the stated inputs.",
                "citation": "Cohen, J.D., and Deeming, J.E. (1985). The National Fire-Danger Rating System: The Ignition Component. General Technical Report INT-188. Ogden, UT: U.S. Department of Agriculture, Forest Service, Intermountain Forest and Range Experiment Station. 26 p."
            },
